  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q6-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "A right-angled triangle has cosine ratio of $\\frac{1}{2}$. Every side of the triangle is made 3 times longer. What is the new cosine ratio? Explain your answer using a diagram if necessary.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{1}{2}$. The triangles are similar, so the cosine ratio is unchanged.",
      "worked": "Let $A$ be the adjacent side and $H$ the hypotenuse.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{New cosine ratio}&=\\frac{3A}{3H}\\\\&=\\frac{A}{H}\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe triangles are similar. Multiplying every side by the same factor leaves the ratio unchanged.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 35
  },
